        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Momence%2C_Illinois"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "After the Civil War, a modern railroad crossed the Kankakee River at Momence, linking the town to regional trade.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://cityofmomence.com/history.aspx"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "During the Depression, Momence celebrated its 100th anniversary with the Gladiolas Festival, a tradition that still thrives today.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://cityofmomence.com/history.aspx"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 1909, a soldier’s monument was erected at Central School to honor local men from the 42nd, 76th, 113th infantry and 4th Illinois Cavalry.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://momencegrahamhistorichouse.com/stories-about-momence"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "In July 1893, Indiana crews cut a shallow channel through a limestone ledge east of Momence, draining the Grand Kankakee Marsh.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
